{#
One cluster, as it appears in any view.

A single line: the calendar's colour, the time, then the title taking whatever
is left. Time first because in a dense grid that is the column you scan — the
title is what you read once you have found the row. `g:i a` matches how the
mail list writes times; the grid drops the meridiem to save the width and keeps
it in the tooltip.

Accepts:
  cluster   OccurrenceCluster — the occurrences that draw this one chip
  showTime  whether to print the start time (default true; never for all-day)

**A cluster of one is the ordinary case and renders exactly as it always did.**
The views hand over clusters rather than occurrences so there is one code path
for them, not because most chips are merged — almost none are. Everything below
normalises onto `occurrence` and `event`, which is what the markup reads.

A cluster of several is one meeting that legitimately exists twice: extracted
from its invitation onto the account's calendar, and mirrored from the provider
onto a connected one, both carrying the organiser's UID. Its dot is a
conic-gradient of the member calendars' colours in equal slices — the same
1.5×1.5 dot, so the row's rhythm does not change — and the tooltip names the
calendars, because a two-tone dot says "more than one" and nothing else. The
slice arithmetic is done here rather than on the DTO: it is a CSS value, and
the DTO carries the colours a chip may draw with, not the way it draws them.

`text-left` is not decoration. This is a <button>, and a button centres its text
by default, which is what had every chip in the month grid sitting oddly
mid-cell.

Opens the editor in the body-level modal frame — never inside the calendar
pane, which carries backdrop-filter and would clip a fixed-position dialog to
itself. The controller has to be on the trigger: a Stimulus action only reaches
controllers mounted on an ancestor, and the modal's lives on #modal-backdrop.

**This is the only place an editor is opened on an occurrence**, and it is why
the three views include this partial rather than each writing their own button.
The URL carries `instance` — the occurrence's recurrence id, which is where the
rule ORIGINALLY put it, not where an override may since have moved it — because
without it the editor knows the event and not which of its occurrences was
clicked, and "this event" has nothing to key a patch on. UTC, and read back by
EventInstanceEditor::instance(), which owns both directions of that spelling.

The URL names the PRIMARY member's event, and only that one. The editor
re-derives the rest of the cluster from that event's uid, so no cluster
identity is threaded through a URL that would outlive the render that made it.
#}

{% set occurrence = cluster.primary %}
{% set event = occurrence.event %}
{% set showTime = showTime|default(true) and not event.isAllDay %}

{% set chip_title = event.title ~ (showTime ? ' · ' ~ occurrence.startsAt|date('g:i a') : '') %}

{% if cluster.isMerged %}
    {% set chip_title = chip_title ~ ' · ' ~ 'calendar.chip.on_calendars'|trans({
        '%calendars%': cluster.calendarNames|join(', '),
    }) %}

    {% set slices = [] %}
    {% for color in cluster.colors %}
        {% set slices = slices|merge([
            color
                ~ ' ' ~ (loop.index0 * 100 / cluster.colors|length)|round(3) ~ '%'
                ~ ' ' ~ (loop.index * 100 / cluster.colors|length)|round(3) ~ '%',
        ]) %}
    {% endfor %}

    {% set dot_style = 'background: conic-gradient(' ~ slices|join(', ') ~ ')' %}
{% else %}
    {% set dot_style = 'background-color: ' ~ event.calendar.color %}
{% endif %}

<button type="button"
   data-controller="ui--modal"
   data-action="click->ui--modal#open"
   data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_calendar_event_edit', {
       id: event.id,
       instance: occurrence.recurrenceId|date('Y-m-d\\TH:i:s\\Z', 'UTC'),
   }) }}"
   data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ 'calendar.event.title'|trans }}"
   title="{{ chip_title }}"
   class="w-full text-left flex items-center gap-1.5
          px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-md
          hover:bg-hover transition-colors min-w-0
          focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent
          {{ occurrence.cancelled ? 'opacity-50' : '' }}"
>
    <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full shrink-0"
          style="{{ dot_style }}"
          aria-hidden="true"></span>

    {% if showTime %}
        <span class="shrink-0 text-[11px] tabular-nums text-ink-faint">
            {{ occurrence.startsAt|date('g:i') }}
        </span>
    {% endif %}

    <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-xs text-ink
                 {{ occurrence.cancelled ? 'line-through' : '' }}">
        {%- if event.kind is not null -%}
            <i class="{{ event.kind.icon }} mr-1 text-[10px] text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        {%- endif -%}
        {{ event.title }}
    </span>
</button>
